schema HumanExperienceObservation
generation control-1
authority native-kernel
fiber HumanExperienceGraph
note A graph fiber over the same Resource identity as Work and Relationship. Records measured human outcomes of an inhabited computational workplace, so that criticism from researchers becomes computable evidence rather than remembered advice.

field id
  type u64
  role identity
  generated true

field actor
  type text
  required true
  role actor-resource-id

field scope
  type text
  note run, room, session or institution the observation belongs to

field activity
  type text
  note what the person was doing; an observation without a task is hard to interpret

field measure
  type enum
  values social_connection belonging loneliness attention interruption cognitive_load stress agency autonomy control trust trust_calibration anthropomorphism felt_understanding flow engagement meaning affect task_satisfaction human_human_contact human_ai_contact productivity_self_report productivity_observed
  required true

field instrument
  type text
  required true
  note the validated scale or observable used. An observation with no instrument is an opinion

field value
  type real
  required true

field temporal_window
  type text
  required true
  note observations without a window cannot be compared

field intervention
  type text
  note which condition produced this, e.g. habitat-spatial, habitat-social-agents, conventional-surface

field comparison
  type text
  note the condition this is measured against

field evidence_ref
  type text
  required true

invariant no-composite-score
  statement measures are never summed or averaged into a single wellbeing number
  derived-from the same law that keeps realized cash separate from pipeline

invariant no-inferred-affect
  statement emotional state is never inferred from behaviour; only instrumented self-report or an observable counts
  note "19 context transitions in 22 minutes" is an observation. "seems stressed" is not

invariant instrument-required
  statement a measure without a named instrument is not admissible as evidence

invariant intervention-needs-comparison
  statement a value attributed to an intervention carries the condition it is compared against

principle human-connection-preservation
  statement AI-mediated social presence must not silently substitute for human connection where human connection is materially valuable
  applies-to ProviderGraph selection
  example answer a factual question -> AI is appropriate
  example resolve an ambiguous conflict with a coworker -> facilitate human contact

axis cognitive-cooling
  statement a cooled subject must also be visually, socially and cognitively quiet
  note cooling previously meant only computational quiet; in an inhabited surface it must also mean not glowing, pulsing, moving or holding central attention
  reheat same condition as the computational axis
